  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Women-Owned Small Business (WOSB) set-aside obligations in FY2026 to date total $769M. The federal government made 2,338 awards, with an average award size of $329K. Obligations are down 39.6% year over year, and current-year totals are partial because fiscal year to date figures are not yet complete. Department of Defense leads buying with $364M in obligations, followed by Department of Homeland Security with $88.9M and Department of Health and Human Services with $67.7M. Other buying agencies with notable activity include Department of Commerce with $66.1M and Department of Justice with $32.3M. Other Computer Related Services and Engineering Services are the largest industries by obligations, with $147M and $133M respectively. Top vendors in FY2026 to date include FCN, INC. with $19.7M and STRATEGIC ALLIANCE BUSINESS GROUP LLC with $18.9M. These figures reflect obligations through the current fiscal year to date only and do not represent a full fiscal year total.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What do FY2026 WOSB set-aside totals show?",
        "body": "The federal government obligated $769M to WOSB set-asides in FY2026 to date. The federal government issued 2,338 awards at an average award size of $329K. Obligations are down 39.6% year over year, and current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is not complete."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where are WOSB obligations concentrated by agency and industry?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $364M, making it the largest buying agency for WOSB set-asides in FY2026 to date. Other Computer Related Services and Engineering Services are the largest industries, with $147M and $133M in obligations respectively. Department of Homeland Security obligated $88.9M and Department of Health and Human Services obligated $67.7M, while Department of Commerce obligated $66.1M."
      }
    ]
  },
